  "spectral_note": "Measured 2026-08-14, over a 20 s window from 60 s, as band energy above a swept 6-pole highpass: -55.4 dB at 14 kHz, -58.6 at 16 k, -63.4 at 18 k, -67.5 at 19 k, -74.1 at 20 k, -78.9 at 20.5 k. A SMOOTH ROLL-OFF WITH NO BRICKWALL -- no step in that series is the sudden 20+ dB cliff a low-rate lossy upstream leaves. Consistent with a healthy 48 kHz Opus rung reaching ~20 kHz, so ~20 kHz is recorded as the cutoff rather than flagged as damage. The tenet asks for this number to be written down; it was missing when this record was created.",
  "notes": "Used as the PROLOGUE's picture and score (built by scripts/build_prologue.py), not as a bed under other footage. DELIVERED LEVEL, measured on the decoded deliverable: the prologue master is gated by tools/peaks.py to -1.1 dBTP, inside the -0.9..-1.1 band. Gating it is not optional: this is where issue #82's systemic miss bites, a lossless master left ungated because only the lossy copy ever was. THE OPENING CARRIES A LEVEL RIDE, and it is level, not dynamics: the owner reported the opening sparks as 'jarring audio for the audience'. Measured, they hit ~0 dBFS against a bed at -13..-18 dB RMS, and the source master is clipped before this project touches it (decoded samples reach +1.9 dBFS). A limiter or compressor would have rewritten the dynamics Nightwish mixed, so scripts/build_prologue.py rides the LEVEL instead: -12 dB at the head, reaching unity at 15.0 s, after the 12.2-12.5 s broadband burst. Every transient is intact; none of them arrives at full scale."
